cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "coderateopt: availability-constrained code-rate and MODCOD selection on a fading optical link"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-06
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Code-rate and MODCOD selection on a fading optical link, treated as the
  constrained optimisation it is: maximise expected goodput over a discrete
  MODCOD set subject to a stated availability target, with both readings of
  that target -- every interval meeting it, or the long-run average meeting it
  -- written down and priced against each other. Marginal fade models
  (lognormal, gamma-gamma, empirical) supply the per-MODCOD delivery
  probability. The discrete problem is solved by scipy.optimize.milp with the
  relative MIP gap set to zero and the continuous part re-solved exactly on the
  chosen support, and cross-checked against subset enumeration and a
  solver-free closed form for two-entry mixes. The stability interval of the
  chosen MODCOD in the scintillation index, the margin or the target is
  resolved by bisection, separating knife-edge optima from flat ones.
  Infeasible instances raise with the margin that would fix them; ties are
  resolved canonically and reported. Validation level 2, research grade. Not
  flight-qualified, not certified, not approved for operational aerospace use.
authors:
  - name: "OPTIMA Organisation"
keywords:
  - free-space-optical
  - modcod-selection
  - code-rate
  - link-availability
  - mixed-integer-programming
  - scintillation
  - sensitivity-analysis
  - goodput
references:
  - type: book
    authors:
      - family-names: Andrews
        given-names: "L. C."
      - family-names: Phillips
        given-names: "R. L."
    title: "Laser Beam Propagation through Random Media"
    edition: "2nd"
    publisher:
      name: "SPIE Press"
    year: 2005
    notes: >-
      Source of the lognormal irradiance model and of the scintillation index
      definition used in coderateopt.fade.
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Al-Habash
        given-names: "M. A."
      - family-names: Andrews
        given-names: "L. C."
      - family-names: Phillips
        given-names: "R. L."
    title: >-
      Mathematical model for the irradiance probability density function of a
      laser beam propagating through turbulent media
    journal: "Optical Engineering"
    volume: 40
    issue: 8
    year: 2001
    notes: >-
      Source of the gamma-gamma irradiance model. The moment identities used
      here are verified numerically in validation/validate_fade_moments.py
      rather than taken on trust; no page number is quoted because none was
      verified in this environment.
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Goldsmith
        given-names: "A. J."
      - family-names: Chua
        given-names: "S.-G."
    title: "Variable-rate variable-power MQAM for fading channels"
    journal: "IEEE Transactions on Communications"
    volume: 45
    issue: 10
    year: 1997
    notes: >-
      Named as the adaptive-rate framing this problem sits in. No result of
      that paper is reimplemented here.
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Huangfu
        given-names: "Q."
      - family-names: Hall
        given-names: "J. A. J."
    title: "Parallelizing the dual revised simplex method"
    journal: "Mathematical Programming Computation"
    volume: 10
    issue: 1
    year: 2018
    notes: >-
      HiGHS, the solver behind scipy.optimize.milp and scipy.optimize.linprog
      as used here.
  - type: standard
    title: "Prediction method of fade dynamics on Earth-space paths"
    number: "ITU-R P.1623"
    institution:
      name: "International Telecommunication Union"
    notes: >-
      Named as the methodology for fade-duration and fade-dynamics statistics.
      NOT implemented in this repository, which models the marginal fade
      distribution only.
  - type: standard
    title: >-
      Propagation data and prediction methods required for the design of
      Earth-space telecommunication systems
    number: "ITU-R P.618"
    institution:
      name: "International Telecommunication Union"
    notes: >-
      Named as the propagation-availability methodology whose outputs this
      repository consumes. NOT implemented here.
